mpv-dmo (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sparky Stereo OS build of deb-multimedia's mpv-dmo @DMOVERSION@ with
    its packaging otherwise unchanged, plus thirty-two patches for stereo 3D
    video, built against the ffmpeg-dmo @FFMPEG@ libraries.
  * Eight patches are upstream commits after 0.41.0 that the others build on:
    the stereo 3D layout read from the stream's frame side data and the
    bitstream's layout preferred over the container tag (upstream pull
    request 18490 and its follow-ups), and the on-screen display drawn once
    per eye in vo_gpu_next.
  * Twenty-four patches add 3D video support for the stereo desktop: an
    automatic filter that unpacks 3D video (frame packing SEI, Matroska
    StereoMode) to full side by side, the declaration of the video surface
    to KWin through libstereo-declare, separate layers for the video and the
    on-screen controls with gpu and gpu-next (Vulkan and OpenGL) on Wayland,
    each eye's picture in the middle of its own view, interpolation of each
    view from its own frames, and how a 360 or VR180 video maps its sphere
    as track-list/N/demux-projection.
  * debian/control, debian/rules: build with libstereo-declare-dev
    (-Dstereo-declare=enabled), libmpv-dev depends on it as mpv.pc requires it.

 -- Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

